@meta
id: 30-14
title: Drill — take it back
chapter: 30
type: drill
skills: git-in-vim
par: 71
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: clicking three revert arrows in the diff gutter
open: config.development.ts

@brief
Three lines of local fiddling in a config file that were never meant to
leave your machine. `config.development.ts.orig` is the committed
version, provided with the lesson, and does not change.

Eight times: split it against the original, walk the changes, take each
one back, save and quit.

@keys
| `:vert diffsplit file` | the two versions, side by side |
| `Ctrl-W l` | into the right-hand window — yours |
| `]c` | next change |
| `do` | take the other side's version |

@hints
The new window opens on the left with the cursor in it. Move right
before you start obtaining, or you will be editing the copy.
--
`]c` `do` three times, then `:wqa`.

@solution
    :vert diffsplit config.development.ts.orig<Enter>  Ctrl-W l
    ]c do  ]c do  ]c do  :wqa<Enter>

The muscle being built is the pairing: `]c` to arrive, `do` to decide,
never scrolling and never retyping a line by hand. Retyping is how a
"revert" quietly introduces a fourth change.

@start config.development.ts
export const config = {
  database: {
    host: 'localhost',
    port: 3306,
  },
  payment: {
    endpoint: 'https://sandbox.payments.local/v2',
    timeout: 60000,
  },
  logging: {
    level: 'trace',
  },
};

@expected config.development.ts
export const config = {
  database: {
    host: 'database',
    port: 3306,
  },
  payment: {
    endpoint: 'https://sandbox.payments.local/v2',
    timeout: 5000,
  },
  logging: {
    level: 'info',
  },
};

@start config.development.ts.orig
export const config = {
  database: {
    host: 'database',
    port: 3306,
  },
  payment: {
    endpoint: 'https://sandbox.payments.local/v2',
    timeout: 5000,
  },
  logging: {
    level: 'info',
  },
};
